      Vanilla Cream Frappuccino
         Mango Passion Tea

257
00:16:25,490 --> 00:16:27,310
<i>Are these even drinks?</i>

258
00:16:27,310 --> 00:16:30,180
<i>My coffee bean knowledge 
doesn't even matter here!</i>

259
00:16:30,180 --> 00:16:31,730
<i>Also, it's so expensive!</i>

260
00:16:31,730 --> 00:16:35,770
<i>I only have 580 yen left over 
after I splurged the other day.</i>

261
00:16:35,770 --> 00:16:38,520
<i>The sandwiches look good too, but...</i>

262
00:16:35,770 --> 00:16:38,520
Teriyaki Green Sandwich                  Yen

263
00:16:35,770 --> 00:16:38,520
Yen

264
00:16:35,770 --> 00:16:38,520
Egg Salad Sandwich

265
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:40,940
You might like this one, Yukiya.

266
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:45,240
We have 9 varieties of
milk to choose from at
the same price!

267
00:16:41,470 --> 00:16:43,070
Right.

268
00:16:43,070 --> 00:16:45,240
<i>I guess I could afford this.</i>

269
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:47,680
This one, then.

270
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:48,310
Yes, sir.

271
00:16:48,310 --> 00:16:50,720
Would you like it iced or hot?

272
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:52,460
Iced.

273
00:16:54,410 --> 00:16:56,710
Okay, I'll have...

274
00:16:56,710 --> 00:16:59,320
One grande Matcha Strawberry Frappe 
with extra matcha powder,

275
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:02,150
and added chocolate chips 
and chocolate sauce.

276
00:17:02,150 --> 00:17:03,810
And then...

277
00:17:04,260 --> 00:17:06,510
I like 
your pigtails

278
00:17:06,510 --> 00:17:07,080
<i>What?</i>

279
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:09,760
<i>Does she actually eat this much?</i>

280
00:17:09,760 --> 00:17:12,520
You were so stiff, Yukiya.

281
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:13,520
I get it.

282
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:17,540
Coming to Starparty after school 
with such a cute girl...

283
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:19,470
It's just a coffee shop.

284
00:17:19,470 --> 00:17:22,060
It isn't any different
 from boss's place.

285
00:17:22,060 --> 00:17:23,790
Stare.

286
00:17:23,790 --> 00:17:25,030
What?

287
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:28,990
Such. A. Cute. Girl.

288
00:17:28,990 --> 00:17:31,400
Shush. I heard you. I'm ignoring you.

289
00:17:31,790 --> 00:17:33,540
I like 
your pigtails

290
00:17:34,270 --> 00:17:37,050
It's so matcha-y!

291
00:17:37,880 --> 00:17:41,420
Chiffon cakes are so spongy.

292
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:45,390
Yukiya, remember when 
you saw earl gray cupcakes

293
00:17:45,390 --> 00:17:48,010
and you asked, 
"does this have pepper in it?"

294
00:17:48,010 --> 00:17:50,390
<i>She seems awful happy today.</i>

295
00:17:50,390 --> 00:17:52,570
It was ganache-flavored until recently.

296
00:17:52,570 --> 00:17:53,600
Yeah?

297
00:17:53,600 --> 00:17:54,640
Do you know what ganache is?

298
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:55,830
Of course I do!

299
00:17:56,490 --> 00:17:58,370
Speaking of ganache,

300
00:17:58,370 --> 00:18:01,530
I went to have cake with Akane 
and Nacchan the other day...

301
00:17:58,370 --> 00:18:01,530
<i>Miku's grinning all the time.</i>

302
00:18:01,530 --> 00:18:07,350
And there was this ganache cake that 
said it used chocolate from Hokkaido.

303
00:18:01,530 --> 00:18:05,440
<i>She's always going on about 
trivial stuff with so much joy.</i>

304
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:10,870
<i>I like seeing her talking so happily.</i>

305
00:18:07,350 --> 00:18:10,870
So then, when I saw ganache, 
I started craving it, and...

306
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:17,530
Man, I'm pretty full.

307
00:18:17,530 --> 00:18:18,560
I bet.

308
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:20,580
I figured you could never finish it.

309
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:22,050
You can have it, Yukiya.

310
00:18:22,050 --> 00:18:25,370
But you bought it for yourself.

311
00:18:25,370 --> 00:18:26,600
It's yummy.

312
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:27,920
Eat it.

313
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:34,320
Wow!

314
00:18:35,660 --> 00:18:39,230
Right? I knew you'd like that.

315
00:18:42,650 --> 00:18:44,100
<i>Did she...</i>

316
00:18:45,320 --> 00:18:49,120
<i>I made him spend so much 
money the other day.</i>

317
00:18:49,750 --> 00:18:56,080
<i>I wanted to repay him, but this 
guy never just accepts things.</i>

318
00:18:56,660 --> 00:18:59,290
<i>He's such a pain.</i>

319
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,490
<i>You didn't need to bother.</i>

320
00:19:08,620 --> 00:19:11,000
It says something there.

321
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,340
Hm? This?

322
00:19:12,340 --> 00:19:14,600
I like 
your pigtails

323
00:19:13,850 --> 00:19:15,480
What is this?

324
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:17,830
Who would write this?

325
00:19:17,830 --> 00:19:19,290
The barista.

326
00:19:19,290 --> 00:19:21,530
They write things once in a while.

327
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,010
What's wrong?

328
00:19:25,010 --> 00:19:27,020
What is it?

329
00:19:27,450 --> 00:19:30,320
I'm just cringing because it's so shallow.

330
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:32,550
It says something on yours, too.

331
00:19:33,620 --> 00:19:36,620
You make a wonderful couple

332
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:41,180
Oh? Uh-huh.

333
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:44,880
I guess that's how people see us, huh?

334
00:19:46,010 --> 00:19:49,820
People think we're a couple. 
How do you feel about that?

335
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:51,060
What do you mean?

336
00:19:51,060 --> 00:19:52,030
I don't mind.

337
00:19:52,030 --> 00:19:54,530
Oh. Okay.

338
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:57,280
This legit makes me happy, though.

339
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:58,690
Maybe because it's hand-written.

340
00:19:58,690 --> 00:20:00,500
It's a bit touching, isn't it?

341
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:02,280
Yeah, I guess.

342
00:20:09,890 --> 00:20:10,880
Here.

343
00:20:14,530 --> 00:20:15,570
It's beautiful when you go from
pouting to smiling.
                                                      Miku

344
00:20:15,570 --> 00:20:17,780
It's beautiful when you go from
pouting to smiling.
                                                      Miku

345
00:20:19,290 --> 00:20:22,330
It's beautiful when you go from
pouting to smiling.
                                                      
                                      Miku

346
00:20:20,100 --> 00:20:22,330
Did your heart skip a beat?

347
00:20:22,860 --> 00:20:24,240
Over what?

348
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,920
Over this piece of paper

349
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:29,240
that says "It's beautiful when 
you go from pouting to smiling"?

350
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,780
Don't read it out loud!

351
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:33,100
Fine, I have one for you too, then.

352
00:20:40,530 --> 00:20:41,570
What is this?

353
00:20:41,570 --> 00:20:43,440
You can't tell?

354
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:44,460
It's you.

355
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:45,770
Huh? It's me?

356
00:20:45,770 --> 00:20:47,390
You're so childlike,

357
00:20:47,390 --> 00:20:50,060
yet you have the mind to hide 
your hairband under your hair.

358
00:20:50,610 --> 00:20:53,520
That's the essence of your pigtails.

359
00:20:53,860 --> 00:20:56,500
It looks good on you, Miku.

360
00:20:58,350 --> 00:21:01,770
<i>Yukiya drew me.</i>

361
00:21:01,770 --> 00:21:03,360
<i>Even though he can't draw.</i>

362
00:21:03,900 --> 00:21:07,150
Wait, did you seriously draw that 
on the back of the receipt?!

363
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:12,330
I'm headed to the bathroom.

364
00:21:12,330 --> 00:21:13,510
'Kay.

365
00:21:28,350 --> 00:21:31,860
It's beautiful when you go from
pouting to smiling.
                                             Miku

366
00:21:52,250 --> 00:21:55,010
To be continued

367
00:23:25,010 --> 00:23:40,220
Next Time
My Childhood Friend Comes In the Morning

368
00:23:26,050 --> 00:23:27,900
Do you ever go to 
the convenience store at night?

369
00:23:27,900 --> 00:23:31,190
There's just something reassuring about 
that glaring light in the night, right?

370
00:23:31,190 --> 00:23:36,410
I think it's written in our DNA that 
we should find comfort in the campfire.

371
00:23:36,410 --> 00:23:38,590
Next episode: "My Childhood Friend 
Comes In the Morning."

